Build node's V8 API from the visor v8 shim instead of the bundled V8.

configure.py's --without-bundled-v8 already drops every deps/v8 build target
and the deps/v8/include search path, but two references to V8's own archives
survive in the link line: node.gyp whole-archives libv8_base_without_compiler
and node.gypi whole-archives <(v8_base), which is libv8_snapshot. Neither
archive is built in that configuration, so the first reference goes away and
the second is gated on node_use_bundled_v8 along with the rest of the
bundled-V8 build.

What stands in their place is the shim's own translation units, staged into
deps/v8shim by the recipe and compiled into libnode itself rather than into
an archive of their own: they include src/env.h and its closure, so they
need exactly the include and define set node.gyp already composes for node's
own sources. Their two include roots arrive in CPPFLAGS.

--- a/node.gyp
+++ b/node.gyp
@@ -660,7 +660,6 @@
               'ldflags': [
                 '-Wl,--whole-archive',
                 '<(obj_dir)/<(STATIC_LIB_PREFIX)<(node_core_target_name)<(STATIC_LIB_SUFFIX)',
-                '<(obj_dir)/tools/v8_gypfiles/<(STATIC_LIB_PREFIX)v8_base_without_compiler<(STATIC_LIB_SUFFIX)',
                 '-Wl,--no-whole-archive',
               ],
             }],
--- a/node.gypi
+++ b/node.gypi
@@ -318,7 +318,7 @@
       ],
     }],
     [ '(OS=="freebsd" or OS=="linux" or OS=="openharmony") and node_shared=="false"'
-        ' and force_load=="true"', {
+        ' and force_load=="true" and node_use_bundled_v8=="true"', {
       'ldflags': [
         '-Wl,-z,noexecstack',
         '-Wl,--whole-archive <(v8_base)',
